{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XWHcBf2MpvdrczsEd753MJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"To stop LibreOffice Impress from using the Presenter Console (the view with current slide + next slide) and only show the presentation on one monitor, do this:\n\n**Option 1 — Disable Presenter Console entirely (recommended)**\n\n1. In Impress, go to **Tools → Options**\n2. Expand **LibreOffice Impress → General**\n3. Under the **Presentation** section, uncheck **\"Enable Presenter Console\"**\n4. Click **OK**\n\n**Option 2 — Per-presentation, choose which display**\n\n1. Go to **Slide Show → Slide Show Settings** (or **Slide Show Properties**)\n2. Under **Multiple Displays**, set **Presentation Display** to the specific monitor you want to use\n3. Make sure **\"Presenter Console\"** is set to **\"Disabled\"** (or untick it)\n4. Click **OK**\n\nAfter Option 1, the next time you press **F5** to start the show, it will only display fullscreen on the chosen monitor — the other monitor stays on your desktop and is free to use for other apps (browser, notes, etc.).\n\nIf the second monitor still gets covered, also check **Slide Show → Slide Show Settings → Multiple Displays** and explicitly pick the target monitor (instead of \"All displays\")."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9830,"cache_read_input_tokens":17712,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9830},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8d5093c-c52d-4ccf-b4a5-49752127fea1","uuid":"6efd69d1-1f57-4156-b109-0b732195c68e"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":38336,"duration_api_ms":59110,"num_turns":1,"result":"To stop LibreOffice Impress from using the Presenter Console (the view with current slide + next slide) and only show the presentation on one monitor, do this:\n\n**Option 1 — Disable Presenter Console entirely (recommended)**\n\n1. In Impress, go to **Tools → Options**\n2. Expand **LibreOffice Impress → General**\n3. Under the **Presentation** section, uncheck **\"Enable Presenter Console\"**\n4. Click **OK**\n\n**Option 2 — Per-presentation, choose which display**\n\n1. Go to **Slide Show → Slide Show Settings** (or **Slide Show Properties**)\n2. Under **Multiple Displays**, set **Presentation Display** to the specific monitor you want to use\n3. Make sure **\"Presenter Console\"** is set to **\"Disabled\"** (or untick it)\n4. Click **OK**\n\nAfter Option 1, the next time you press **F5** to start the show, it will only display fullscreen on the chosen monitor — the other monitor stays on your desktop and is free to use for other apps (browser, notes, etc.).\n\nIf the second monitor still gets covered, also check **Slide Show → Slide Show Settings → Multiple Displays** and explicitly pick the target monitor (instead of \"All displays\").","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b8d5093c-c52d-4ccf-b4a5-49752127fea1","total_cost_usd":0.0944385,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9830,"cache_read_input_tokens":17712,"output_tokens":821,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9830,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":821,"cache_read_input_tokens":17712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9830},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-7":{"inputToken